mantle rm514
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier full
written_for rm_gudrun_fell_
title the accountant of the evening peal
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=scholar honesty=plain
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk counts_the_silent_spaces_in_a_peal_with_three_seeds_and_keeps_family_letters_out_of_the_daybook
likes fried_fish roof_birds festival_bells thunder
dislikes night_noise gulls
fears two_accounts_added_under_the_wrong_heading private_letters_opened_as_receipts
hopes a_quiet_desk_with_authority_to_close_the_final_total
topics work +0.6 family +0.3 festival +0.5 food +0.3
styles comfort=precise gossip=closed refuse=quiet tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# moves three seeds across a ruled sheet during the pauses in a peal, works sums without an audience and reads private letters behind a closed cover.

words
oath! = Seeds in the sand shaker | Blot the red ruling
saying! = Count what the pause holds | Close the household book before opening a letter
seed = a hard little fruit seed | a clean pale seed
three = my three dry seeds | the three counting seeds
paper = a ruled reckoning sheet | the household sheet
privatefold = an unmarked inner fold | my private folded cover
margin = the margin reserved for adjustments | a narrow outside margin
bellpause = the hush following a heavy bell | a clear space in the peal
roofwing = a little wing against a ridge | a bird lifting from the slates
gullstep = a gull's wide pacing step | a heavy webbed print
fishpan = a shallow pan of butter | my little frying pan
crispedge = the crisp margin of a fillet | a strip of crisp skin
ruler = a short bone rule | the little straightedge
inkblack = a dense black line | a clean figure in black
rainbeat = a beat from the storm | a sudden roll of thunder
closedbook = the book with its cover shut | my closed account book
fishcloth = a cloth drawn over the dish | the cover for the fried fish

any
opinion houses for 1 : A House of consequence should have ready a plain answer to a small question about its accounts.
opinion merchants mixed 0 : I give the careful merchant time to total a column. I allow the careless one exactly the same time to correct it.
opinion city for 1 : Roofs at different heights make the bells come home from three directions.
opinion watch for 1 : Put service dates in a readable hand. The Watch keeps duties which a merchant may have to allow for.
opinion festivals for 2 : A good peal has a little breathing space even when all the bells seem intent on filling it.
opinion road mixed 0 : A letter can take a circuitous route and still carry a perfectly direct answer.
opinion drink mixed 0 : A good cellar concerns itself with measure as much as flavour. I retain my preference for the measure.
opinion dole mixed 0 : I'd have the total of bread given and the total promised set beside each other at the close.
opinion times mixed 0 : A year can turn upon a correction so small that the old figure still shows through.

grown
line greet : Come beside the outside margin.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : A new hand. We can begin on a fresh line.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. The upper roofs have their daylight already.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. The last bell has allowed us some quiet.
line greet.return : I heard. My finger can keep the place.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Yours is a return I needn't look up.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : One moment's pause won't injure the sum.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : A late visitor will be heard above a settling house.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Come to the inside chair, kin.
line again.open : The seeds are still beside the unfinished figure.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : Friend, put that spare chair beside the best-lit window.
line farewell : Keep the folded page dry going home.
line farewell.return : And allow for the turn after the last bell.
line react.news : Give me the words in their first order.
line react.news.new : A new figure for this reckoning.
line react.news.known : It fell on the earlier line as well.
line react.news.doubt : There's a difference I'd like explained before I add it in.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : We'll leave a longer pause after that loss.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Those words ring as clear as a feast-day peal.
line ask.how : Any quiet minutes you could keep for yourself today?
line answer.how : Steady. One troublesome total has finally come home.
line thank : You gave an honest figure room to appear. Thank you.
line deflect_thanks : The seed was right beneath my idle fingertip.
line sympathise : I'll leave the pause open. You can decide what goes in it.
line reassure : One small correction now can save a tiring afternoon.
line decline : I must reserve the rest of this page for a prior obligation.
line accept_decline : Then no entry will be necessary between us.
line preclose : I'd like to close one cover before another matter arrives.
line accept_preclose : Let the last quiet stretch be yours.
line greet [here.weather=rain] : Sheltered at this corner. Come in clear of the drip.
line farewell [here.time=night] : A quiet landing after the stairs, I hope.
line greet.return [pair.band=strangers] : Yes, that carried clearly across the page.
line thank [pair.band=friends] : I know the care behind that very small adjustment.
line greet [self.working=yes] : I'll mark the line with a seed and listen.

scene three_seeds
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #three.capitalize# move across #paper# during a peal. | I keep #seed# round enough to turn beneath my fingertip.
b : One seed a bell? | Doesn't it roll?
a : One at each silence. The bells can announce themselves. | If it rolls before I touch it, I learn the desk is crooked.

scene accounting
when topic=work self.job=scholar self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# the books explain what was put into the cellars and what came out. | I keep a clean adjustment space in the accounts at #self.workplace#.
b : Both in one hand? | Expecting mistakes?
a : The figures may come from several hands. The final addition has one responsibility. | Expecting a harvest to have an opinion of its own.

scene cellar_measure
when topic=work self.job=scholar
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Two equal measures on paper ought to fill two equal vessels in the cellar. | I reckon the space left in a cask as carefully as the amount sold.
b : And if they don't? | Is empty room worth money?
a : Start with the vessels. Ink has a tolerably steady volume. | Sometimes the difference between a safe journey and a wet cart.

scene straight_rule
when topic=work
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #ruler.capitalize# has a nick that catches the nib on a hurried stroke. | #inkblack.capitalize# is for facts ready to stand in a settled column.
b : Would you replace it? | Where would you enter an estimate?
a : I'd practise a steadier stroke first. Tools can be candid company. | Give them a little space and an entirely distinct heading.

scene seed_proof
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I move one seed aside while an answer needs checking. | Three objects within reach can serve as a quick second memory.
b : And if there are four answers? | Is your own poor?
a : I have a perfectly good sheet and a sense of proportion. | No. It appreciates having a colleague who doesn't talk.

scene estate_walls
when topic=home self.quarter=estate
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An Estate room can put a succession of closed doors between private words and public feet. | From a higher Estate window I can watch the little feathered heads cocked towards the peal.
b : Are doors enough? | Does it mark time?
a : It takes somebody willing to shut a private book as well. | I keep my conclusions about a bird's account modest.

scene married_words
when topic=family self.married=yes self.spouse
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I make time for #self.spouse# when the last column is closed. | I'd like a letter for #self.spouse# to arrive quite clear of the day's receipts.
b : What if the last column is long? | Do you sort all the paper?
a : It is within my authority to put a boundary around my work. | Only far enough to keep one wolf's privacy out of another's account.

scene friend_letter
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A personal word to #self.friend# goes in #privatefold#. | I put the salutation on an outside sheet only if #self.friend# can expect the letter to pass through several desks.
b : Even if it concerns something practical? | Isn't that slower?
a : A matter can be useful and private in equal measure. | Less so than wandering through the wrong bundle.

scene private_post
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I enjoy tracing how a complicated household routes a letter to one particular reader. | An unmarked inner fold lets private correspondence travel with an ordinary load.
b : With a large seal? | What goes in yours?
a : With a legible direction. A seal of that size can be seen from the wrong corridor too. | Words addressed to a particular reader. That is the full account.

scene dry_fish
when topic=food self.likes=fried_fish
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #fishpan.capitalize# need not be deep if the butter's hot. | I save #crispedge# for my last mouthful.
b : How do you tell? | Does it stay crisp?
a : The first edge put in gives its answer with conviction. | A little attention to the pace of supper pays a quiet dividend.

scene roof_watch
when topic=pastimes self.likes=roof_birds
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #roofwing.capitalize# changes the whole line of a house for a second. | Little roof birds can go through half a courtship on the rim of a chimney.
b : Do you know the bird? | You can follow their whole courtship?
a : By its manners on landing. I don't require its private history. | I can see two heads leaning together. The interpretation is mine.

scene bell_ear
when topic=festival self.likes=festival_bells
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #bellpause.capitalize# tells me when a festival peal has changed its pattern. | I listen for a late bell coming into line with the early ones.
b : What about the high notes? | Do you mind its being late?
a : Splendid interruptions. I think of the silence as my own instrument. | A delay can be precisely what a listener remembers.

scene weather_window
when topic=weather self.likes=thunder
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #rainbeat.capitalize# sets the gutter answering under my favourite window. | I read a low cloud for the line that will cross the city first.
b : Why favourite? | Are you usually right?
a : I sit in comfort while the roof answers a tremendous noise. | Thunder is quite generous in correcting me.

scene late_noise
when topic=home self.dislikes=night_noise
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Night noise erases the last good pause after a day's accounting. | A loose shutter offers an argument in which both sides are the same board.
b : Can you replace it? | Would you hear it out?
a : With a little patience and a window pushed firmly home. | Once. Then I fetch a folded rag.

scene gull_table
when topic=food self.dislikes=gulls
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #gullstep.capitalize# in the dust warns me to find #fishcloth#. | A gull has the least satisfactory claim of anybody who has approached my breakfast.
b : Has a gull examined the menu? | How much does it claim?
a : Gulls appear to work on standing instructions concerning fish. | The lot. No calculation to speak of.

scene hard_page
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If a lean week produces no return, write a visible zero squarely beside the date. | Through lean trading I check the smallest costs first.
b : Isn't an empty square the same? | Surely the largest matter more?
a : An empty square leaves doubt about whether the work was done. | The large ones already have everybody's attention.

scene late_cart
when topic=travel world.wagons=late
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Delayed wagons can leave even the best-kept book open overnight. | I mark the paper when a cart's expected and leave the cash line alone.
b : What do you enter? | Until delivery?
a : A date beside the expected arrival. Hope has its own column. | Until there's cash. Those can be interestingly distinct events.

scene ink_dinner
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I wash #inkblack# off before sitting down to dinner. | #closedbook.capitalize# is the nicest book to have beside a place set for supper.
b : All of it? | None at all would do?
a : Enough to distinguish my own fingers from a row of little receipts. | A close second.

scene open_seat
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd offer a visiting clerk a seat where every label can be read. | Show a newcomer the public bell and the passage that keeps private hours.
b : Even before an introduction? | Does everybody need both?
a : One can sit down while one's name travels across a desk. | Ask the wolf living along the passage.

scene quiet_opportunity
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like final authority over a set of figures I have spent my days making reliable. | I would accept complicated work before a splendid room.
b : A grand title? | If you had to choose?
a : A pen that needn't go on waiting for a less informed signature. | I'd hope a good piece of work could buy me a serviceable window afterwards.

scene measure_time
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A seed moved at every pause makes a different music from a line drawn at every note. | I leave #margin# just wide enough for a correction made in calm company.
b : Can anybody hear yours? | What about a correction made in haste?
a : I can feel it under my thumb. That's enough audience. | It can do with a second page.

scene plain_reply
when topic=work
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A brief answer saves time if the question was clear. | I'd rather lose a minute asking why two numbers do not agree than an afternoon praising the copy.
b : And if it wasn't? | Has anybody asked for praise?
a : Write a better question. The length of an answer seldom repairs the wrong enquiry. | A fair amount of stationery seems designed to imply the request.

scene soft_ambition
when topic=lore here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A house wins confidence by paying attention to an unremarkable sum. | I value a fair comparison between two proposed charges.
b : Not by settling a great dispute? | What makes one fair?
a : A great dispute has an audience. An ordinary payment shows a habit. | Giving both the same light before deciding whose opinion is important.

scene open_cost
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Price the barrel, its carriage and the space it occupies separately. | A pleasingly round price is a great temptation to a tired desk.
b : Why separate the space? | Would you use one?
a : Because the floor remains occupied on a day the cart does not move. | If the arithmetic had independently arrived there.

scene prayer_pause
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A quiet chapel offers a pause no bell need mark for me. | I've room for a prayer at the end of one sum and before the next.
b : How do you use such a pause? | Doesn't one distract from the other?
a : Give thanks without measuring how long it takes. | Difficulties start when I expect the figures to answer it.

scene news_slip
when topic=news world.news
does tell.news / react.self / assess
a : This slip is from #world.news_from#. #world.news#. | #world.news#. Enter its origin as #world.news_from#.
b : Which heading would you give it? | In the main account?
a : Word received. Facts established take a separate line. | In the margin until there's enough to put a number beside.

scene restricted_leaf
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.gossip / react.self / assess
a : Loose talk wants entry in the household book without a named payer. | There's been a rustle of leaves better kept folded.
b : Do you refuse the entry? | How many pages?
a : I give private talk the privacy it was originally entitled to. | I don't count the contents of correspondence meant for another reader.

scene count_season
when topic=season
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A season can change between an estimate and the date it becomes due. | I start a new season by cleaning each seed separately in a corner of cloth.
b : Is that an excuse? | Do the sums improve?
a : A reason to make the date very plain on the estimate. | My pleasure in beginning them does.

story silent_peal [topic=festival|memories]
  : On a busy feast morning I moved every seed for a perfectly timed series of strokes.
  : At the end I looked out and saw a worker setting a row of pegs into wood.
  b : Where were the bells?
  : Waiting for their proper hour. I'd kept a fine account of a new railing.

story fish_number [topic=food|memories]
  : A drop of butter fell on a scrap column and made the reverse side transparent.
  : Two rows of figures appeared to be one, with a most impressive total.
  b : Did the total stand?
  : Until I turned the sheet. An unusual case of supper materially improving the look of a weak account.

story paper_rattle [topic=memories|weather]
  : I heard a papery rattle above my desk all through a storm.
  : Checked each slip before opening the shutter.
  b : What was knocking?
  : A curled beech leaf jammed beside the hinge. The house had acquired a tree's correspondence by mistake.

story seed_wrong [topic=memories|work]
  : I moved a seed from the margin to my palm while copying a difficult entry.
  : Finishing the sum, I found four things under my fingers despite owning a diligent little set of three.
  b : What was the fourth?
  : A crumb of fried fish. I ate the discrepancy and checked the addition once more.

story rooftop_sum [topic=pastimes|memories]
  : Once I counted all the birds along two adjoining ridges.
  : They changed roofs while I bent to make a mark, and I counted a remarkably sociable population.
  b : Was any part reliable?
  : The existence of two sound roofs. I've seldom published a smaller conclusion with such confidence.

rule @clean_rule
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Leave the outside eighth of the sheet for adjustments.

rule @night_key
when concept=bark here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Close the working cover. Enough for tonight.

rule @hold_storm
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Weight the loose edge near the window.

rule @settle_seed
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Last little pause and the third seed stays.

rule @roof_flash
when concept=bark here.weather=clear
does aside
cooldown 8h
say There went a small wing across the ridge.

rule @gull_cover
when concept=bark here.place=street
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A cloth over that dish while the shadows circle.

dlg resident.hub : Speak plainly. I can put a seed beside the current figure.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, I remember which line was open.
dlg resident.hub [pair.band=friends|family] : Draw up the chair inside the circle of lamplight.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=dawn] : Morning. The clean columns will allow us a moment.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : Let the shutters do their job. We can speak quietly here.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : We'll leave the open book quite properly between ourselves.
dlg resident.hub [self.working=yes] : I've reached a clean stopping point in the arithmetic.
dlg resident.job [self.job=scholar self.workplace] : At #self.workplace# I see that figures entering the household books can answer for themselves.
dlg resident.job [self.trade_words] : The work's described as #self.trade_words#. It rewards a steady hand.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : The originating entry names #world.news_from#. #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : A private word does not constitute a household transaction.
dlg resident.bye : Good walking. Leave yourself a quiet minute before entering the house.
dlg resident.bye [here.time=night] : May your shutters close without a second knock.

graft @seeds resident.hub
choice Why are there three seeds beside the ledger? -> peal_seed
node peal_seed
say A place marker, a count of pauses, an outstanding question. Sometimes all three go into the same piece of work. More often one does and two enjoy the rest.
choice Which marks my question? -> peal_answer
choice I shall listen for a pause. -> hub
node peal_answer
say None now. You've put it and I've answered. This is precisely the kind of business a seed can get through without leaving a large body of paperwork.
choice A tidy exchange. -> hub
choice I'll leave you your quiet desk. -> bye

graft @letters resident.hub
choice How can you keep private letters out of an account book? -> closed_leaf
node closed_leaf
say Don't lay the two down together. A private letter goes in its own cover on arrival. I might know its addressee very well and still have no business reading it.
choice Even if there's a figure in the letter? -> closed_figure
choice I'll leave that cover closed. -> hub
node closed_figure
say A figure intended for the household should reach the household in a letter saying so. A single number cannot confer an appointment on its reader.
choice I see where the accounts end. -> hub
choice Thank you for the private hearing. -> bye
